    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "So which is better? Neither, in general. A game engine steps time because it has to handle collisions and messy forces. A textbook asks clean questions with exact answers, so solving once is faster and never drifts. The docs don't mention collisions or time steps at all. That absence told me which kind this is.",
